5</sub>, birth campaign 2005.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><p>Variables associated with feeding practices were not associated with increased risk for atypical scrapie (<xref ref-type="table" rid="T4">Table 4</xref>). Feeding milk replacers, which was negatively correlated with dairy production (Spearman coefficient of correlation &#x003c1;&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;&#x02013;0.41, p&#x0003c;0.001), and feeding corn silage showed an inverse association with atypical scrapie.</p><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><title>Univariate analyses of feeding component variables during the specified period and conditional to C<sub>0</sub> for atypical scrapie in sheep, France*</title></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><col width="56" span="1"/><col width="45" span="1"/><col width="45" span="1"/><col width="53" span="1"/><col width="37" span="1"/><thead><tr><th valign="bottom" align="left" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Variable</th><th valign="bottom" align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Controls</th><th valign="bottom" align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cases</th><th valign="bottom" align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Odds ratio</th><th valign="bottom" align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">p value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="5" valign="top" align="left" scope="col" rowspan="1">Lambs fed milk replacers in C<sub>0</sub></td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">	No</td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">68</td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">42</td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.5</td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.02</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">	Yes<hr/></td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">157<hr/></td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="